# Glossary

## AgentPhaseGuide

### Definitions

- A coordinator setup that guides work through Understand, Explore, Make and Evaluate while retaining ownership of the agreed task\. Its instructions guide behavior; they do not enforce runtime switching\.

<details>
<summary>Examples</summary>

- One coordinator loads phase\-appropriate skills and repeats the loop when evaluation reveals more work\.

</details>

### Domain usage

- AgentPhaseGuide

## Agent Essentials

### Definitions

- The always\-on generic rules covering requested\-outcome verification, the phase loop, TDD, boundary mocks, coverage and repository safeguards\.

<details>
<summary>Examples</summary>

- AGENTS\.md applies even when the coordinator agent is not selected\.

</details>

### Domain usage

- AgentPhaseGuide

## Agent Phase

### Definitions

- A named responsibility in the work loop, not necessarily a separate agent or a mandatory formal handoff\.

<details>
<summary>Examples</summary>

- Understand establishes intent; Explore investigates evidence; Make produces the change; Evaluate assesses the result\.

</details>

### Domain usage

- AgentPhaseGuide

## Understand

### Definitions

- The Agent Phase that establishes intent, constraints and observable success conditions, recovering prior context when needed\.

<details>
<summary>Examples</summary>

- Clarify whether a requested glossary split means a derived export or an independently maintained document\.

</details>

### Domain usage

- AgentPhaseGuide

## Explore

### Definitions

- The Agent Phase that inspects evidence, existing code, tests and boundaries, compares options and resolves required approvals before choosing an approach\.

<details>
<summary>Examples</summary>

- Find an existing glossary validator and renderer before introducing export logic\.

</details>

### Domain usage

- AgentPhaseGuide

## Make

### Definitions

- The Agent Phase that produces the agreed change or artifact, including verification during execution\. Production behavior changes follow TDD within this phase\.

<details>
<summary>Examples</summary>

- Write and observe a failing export test before implementing glossary selection\.

</details>

### Domain usage

- AgentPhaseGuide

## Evaluate

### Definitions

- The Agent Phase that compares the result with success conditions, reviews practice compliance separately from test results, records available evidence and decides the next step\.

<details>
<summary>Examples</summary>

- Check that the exported glossary explains the generic setup and excludes project\-specific entries; a passing test suite alone is not that assessment\.

</details>

### Domain usage

- AgentPhaseGuide

## Skill

### Definitions

- An on\-demand set of instructions for a particular activity, loaded when applicable\. Loading a skill is different from delegating to another agent\.

<details>
<summary>Examples</summary>

- The TDD skill guides production behavior changes inside Make; UI design review is loaded only with explicit agreement\.

</details>

### Domain usage

- AgentPhaseGuide

## Coordinator

### Definitions

- The agent role that retains task ownership, scope, authorization, decisions and evidence while selecting applicable capabilities\.

<details>
<summary>Examples</summary>

- Delegating independent research does not transfer responsibility for the requested outcome\.

</details>

### Domain usage

- AgentPhaseGuide

## Handoff

### Definitions

- The transfer of relevant outcomes, evidence, constraints, approvals or next steps between phases or capabilities, without automatically transferring task ownership\.

<details>
<summary>Examples</summary>

- Explore hands Make the chosen approach and required approvals; Make hands Evaluate the change and verification evidence\.

</details>

### Domain usage

- AgentPhaseGuide

## Project Profile

### Definitions

- The project\-specific complement to the generic core, recording safeguards, conventions, paths and commands without embedding them in the portable setup\.

<details>
<summary>Examples</summary>

- The profile supplies test\-framework conventions and, when used, the WorkTask registry and evaluation ledger locations\.

</details>

### Domain usage

- AgentPhaseGuide

## TDD

### Definitions

- Test\-driven development: observe a focused failing test before changing production behavior, implement enough to pass, then review behavior\-preserving improvements with tests green\.

<details>
<summary>Examples</summary>

- Red, Green and Refactor take place inside Make; documentation\-only work does not claim TDD\.

</details>

### Domain usage

- AgentPhaseGuide

## Red

### Definitions

- The TDD step that writes and runs the smallest focused test for one changed behavior and observes its failure before production changes\.

<details>
<summary>Examples</summary>

- An export test fails because no glossary files are produced yet; a compilation failure can also establish Red\.

</details>

### Domain usage

- AgentPhaseGuide

## Green

### Definitions

- The TDD step that implements only enough production behavior to satisfy the focused failing test and verifies that it passes\.

<details>
<summary>Examples</summary>

- Select the approved glossary domain and render the two required export files\.

</details>

### Domain usage

- AgentPhaseGuide

## Refactor

### Definitions

- The TDD step that reviews duplication and cohesion and improves clarity without changing behavior, while keeping tests green\.

<details>
<summary>Examples</summary>

- Extract a real responsibility when useful; do not distort production code to raise coverage\.

</details>

### Domain usage

- AgentPhaseGuide

## Boundary Mock

### Definitions

- A test substitute at an external or system boundary that preserves actual application and domain behavior while controlling boundary results and errors\.

<details>
<summary>Examples</summary>

- Inject an in\-memory filesystem into an export test rather than writing real files or mocking internal selection logic\.

</details>

### Domain usage

- AgentPhaseGuide

## Success Condition

### Definitions

- An observable condition that establishes whether the agreed requested outcome has been achieved\.

<details>
<summary>Examples</summary>

- The export contains only AgentPhaseGuide glossary entries, and its Markdown is derived from the same selected JSON\.

</details>

### Domain usage

- AgentPhaseGuide

## Applicable Default

### Definitions

- A practice followed when applicable, rather than a completion gate; meaningful deviations are briefly justified\.

<details>
<summary>Examples</summary>

- Review meaningful complexity findings without automatically rewriting correct code\.

</details>

### Domain usage

- AgentPhaseGuide

## Safeguard

### Definitions

- A constraint protecting scope, authorization, data, intended behavior or honest verification; it is not an ordinary capability toggle\.

<details>
<summary>Examples</summary>

- Commit only on explicit request with an approved subject; preserve unrelated work\.

</details>

### Domain usage

- AgentPhaseGuide

## Exploration Intent

### Definitions

- A proposed practice whose behavior and scope remain open; it is not active guidance until approved for activation\.

<details>
<summary>Examples</summary>

- A proposed practice is recorded for discussion without authorizing the agent to apply it\.

</details>

### Domain usage

- AgentPhaseGuide

## WorkTask Tracking

### Definitions

- An optional practice that records task progress, decisions, blockers and next steps in a configured registry\. Ask once for a new implementation task without a retained choice; tracking can be changed on request independently of measurement\.

<details>
<summary>Examples</summary>

- A tracked but unmeasured task has a maintained registry entry without a linked measurement evaluation; turning tracking off stops further tracking and measurement without deleting history\.

</details>

### Domain usage

- AgentPhaseGuide

## WorkTask Measurement

### Definitions

- An optional assessment practice for tracked work with a configured evaluation ledger: record whether a task is Measured or NotMeasured, ask separately while Undecided at activation, and retain baseline, outcome evidence and observed metrics\. Measurement requires tracking and can be changed on request\.

<details>
<summary>Examples</summary>

- Turning measurement off leaves task tracking on and preserves earlier evidence; enabling measurement while tracking is off requires agreement to enable tracking first\.

</details>

### Domain usage

- AgentPhaseGuide

## Export Manifest

### Definitions

- The record of exported file paths and the source commit that pins the generic setup's exported content\. It does not establish recipient installation or runtime enforcement\.

<details>
<summary>Examples</summary>

- The export rejects uncommitted source changes so its manifest can identify committed content\.

</details>

### Domain usage

- AgentPhaseGuide

## Runtime Environment

### Definitions

- The environment and APIs in which code executes, distinct from its client/server role and JavaScript execution context\.

<details>
<summary>Examples</summary>

- Runtime Environment \(DevEnv browser client\): Angular application code runs in a browser with browser APIs\.
- Runtime Environment \(DevEnv Node\.js server\): Express application code runs in Node\.js with Node APIs\.
- DevEnv client tests run in Node\.js with a simulated browser environment; being client code does not itself establish a browser runtime\.
- DevEnv diagram validation is runtime\-neutral code: its implementation uses standard JavaScript compatible with both browser and Node\.js environments\. Public exports and transitive dependencies must also be compatible before claiming the shared package is runtime\-neutral\.

</details>

### Domain usage

- DevEnv

